; Terminal consumer of the transitive chain. It consumes BOTH exports via two `--extern-import`
; flags: mid-dep (for `mid_record`) AND base-dep DIRECTLY (for `base_point` / `base_coin`). The
; direct base-dep declaration is the depth-1 rule made concrete — mid-dep's export hides base-dep, so
; a consumer that names a base-dep type must declare base-dep itself.
;
;   * m — a mid-dep type (opaque; itself embeds `base_point`, hidden behind mid_record's class).
;   * b — a base-dep type referenced directly (opaque record).
;   * c — a base-dep transparent alias referenced directly.
;
; A single-file consumer, so `consumer_thing` stays in ROOT_SCOPE. Generated two ways — physical
; stubs for both deps vs two `--extern-import` flags — with byte-identical output the acceptance
; criterion (item 5).
consumer_thing = [m: mid_record, b: base_point, c: base_coin]
